── GATE SWEEP (loosen each gate one notch -> fwd return of the names it NEWLY admits) ──
  positive = the gate was too tight (newly-admitted beat the field); ≤0 = it's keeping junk out.
  the TOO TIGHT flag needs mean AND median positive — one survivor can carry a mean on its own.
  vs shipped = newly-admitted median MINUS the accepted cohort's median (-119.5); >0 = no worse than what the gates already keep.
  growth_min_range_pct -10   admits 0 new names (gate not binding on this sample)
  growth_min_cagr -4         admits 0 new names (gate not binding on this sample)
  growth_min_1y_pct -10      admits 0 new names (gate not binding on this sample)
  max_1m_drop_pct -10 (deeper) admits 0 new names (gate not binding on this sample)
  min_avg_turnover_eur ->0   admits 0 new names (gate not binding on this sample)
  growth_max_above_ma ->off  admits 0 new names (gate not binding on this sample)
  growth_require_lifetime_uptrend ->off admits 0 new names (gate not binding on this sample)
  growth_maxdd_cap ->off     admits 0 new names (gate not binding on this sample)
  growth_min_leg_years ->2 (admits the 2Y rung) admits 0 new names (gate not binding on this sample)
  growth_max_peg ->off       admits 0 new names (gate not binding on this sample)
  growth_min_5y_pct -15      admits 0 new names (gate not binding on this sample)
  growth_min_range_pct_8y -10 (live-only) admits 0 new names (gate not binding on this sample)
